      "kind": "measured",
      "finding": "Original nominal60 adaptive schedule gave Settings median completed intervals16ms and Apps20ms in matched typical gestures; the nominal rate was not a hard start cap."
    },
    {
      "kind": "measured",
      "finding": "With strict60 cap, Settings typical completed moving-frame intervals ranged12.446--19.494ms across the two detailed directions, while Apps ranged17.673--22.095ms."
    },
    {
      "kind": "measured",
      "finding": "Settings slow-release traces in both directions contain about15 consecutive one-pixel steps followed by a stop; generic scroll rounds each low-speed displacement, while Apps has its own row-target ending."
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "finding": "The stripe pipeline writes panel GRAM without a vblank/TE fence. Caps alone do not synchronize panel scanout."
    },
    {
      "kind": "interpretation",
      "finding": "Completion-time variability, integer motion steps and unsynchronized scanout can explain worse perceived motion despite higher throughput. These timings do not identify the physical tear line."
    }
